  "slug": "inference-fit-6a61",
  "summary": "SPHEREx, 21-cm, Lyman-alpha and Euclid papers advance differentiable, emulated or automated components of inference pipelines for upcoming survey analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is building and validating components of survey inference pipelines, with emphasis on differentiable or emulated forward models. Hesperos and Eosphoros provide a GPU-accelerated differentiable forced-photometry operator and forward model for SPHEREx spectrophotometry, while a separate SPHEREx study introduces information-criterion-driven non-linear deprojection of angular imaging systematics, tested on lognormal mocks. A differentiable GPU-accelerated hybrid forward model for global 21-cm cosmology supports uncertainty-quantification benchmarking. Symbolic regression diagnoses a Lyman-alpha GP emulator, and a Sobolev loss improves derivative fidelity for most cases. Lens-Orchestra automates strong-lens forward modeling with LLM agents on 185 Euclid Q1 candidates. The Popcorn Void Finder reimplementation is a reproducibility effort, less directly tied to differentiability.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
